  "id": "COMPOUND:26573 - PROTEIN:5790",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between 6-Hydroxycoumarin and HPAC, mediated through multiple targets. The drug 6-Hydroxycoumarin is identified as a target of SNU-387, which in turn is a target of several compounds, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and Gypenoside Xlvi. All of these compounds ultimately have HPAC as their target. This indicates that 6-Hydroxycoumarin may exert its biological effects through SNU-387, which acts as a bridge to HPAC. The shared target HPAC suggests that these compounds may share a common mechanism of action, possibly involving the modulation of a shared biological pathway or receptor. The evidence supports a pathway where 6-Hydroxycoumarin influences SNU-387, which then interacts with HPAC, highlighting a potential role in the regulation of a shared cellular process. The integration of these findings underscores the importance of SNU-387 as a central mediator in the relationship between 6-Hydroxycoumarin and HPAC.",
